From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: WavJaby <WavJaby@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 10:47:24 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] linux-user: proc/self/maps identity

Under identity mapping (guest_base == 0) guest pointers are host
pointers and the guest runs in the host process. The faked maps and
smaps list only QEMU's guest page regions, so a library the host
dlopened (the GL driver, ANGLE) never appears to the guest. With
guest_base == 0 the open goes to the kernel, which lists the process's
real mappings. guest_base != 0 keeps the fakes: there guest addresses
differ from host ones and the fake is the guest's own view.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [identity mapping is ATL-only]
Patch-Reason: the embedder shares one address space with the host, so QEMU's guest-region view is a partial list of reachable memory; the loader cannot filter what QEMU fakes
---
SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later
 linux-user/syscall.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/linux-user/syscall.c b/linux-user/syscall.c
index 9f454502cb6f6642a57c95f077a9f3d5c38826e2..cc965b06003e040d2cce86eaeafb405779d62488 100644
--- a/linux-user/syscall.c
+++ b/linux-user/syscall.c
@@ -8879,6 +8879,16 @@ static int maybe_do_fake_open(CPUArchState *cpu_env, int dirfd,
     }
 
     for (fake_open = fakes; fake_open->filename; fake_open++) {
+        /*
+         * Identity map (guest_base == 0): guest pointers are host pointers.
+         * The kernel's maps and smaps list the host's libraries too; the
+         * faked ones list only QEMU's guest pages.
+         */
+        if (guest_base == 0 &&
+            (fake_open->fill == open_self_maps ||
+             fake_open->fill == open_self_smaps)) {
+            continue;
+        }
         if (fake_open->cmp(pathname, fake_open->filename)) {
             break;
         }
